  "advancedjei.recipe_tree.help": "The recipe tree shows the crafting flow, total cost, and byproducts.\n\nLeft-click a node to choose a recipe; Shift+left-click can auto-pick from inventory; left-click the category icon to open the current recipe. Multi-input nodes use the + button to open a candidate picker inside the tree. Duplicate input slots are merged, and once a candidate is fixed it applies to every merged slot; when nothing is fixed, all candidates count for inventory, highlighting, and transfer checks, and recursive crafting prefers candidates whose lower-tier ingredients are available.\n\nRight-click folds a node; Shift+right-click clears that recipe for the current tree. Clicking the tree button again on the current recipe also clears it.\n\nCraft mode highlights base materials; the bookmark bar uses red for missing base materials and orange for missing intermediate outputs. Even when items are already available, outputs and materials stay in JEI's bookmark bar. Left-click an intermediate output only inserts direct materials; Shift+left-click recursively crafts only the currently missing steps. Machines with a crafting time only receive materials.\n\nScroll to zoom, drag to pan; scroll on xN to change batch count, and click to pick the batch with the fewest byproducts. Press E, Esc, or the tree button again to go back; right-click the tree button or press Ctrl+C to clear, and R recenters the view.",
